Stopping a thread, by a stop or by taking its process, takes it off its queue or its wait but leaves it in the state it had,
so a woken or resumed one runs in a process that is gone, and a stopped waiter waits on nothing;
a thread without a process is stopped, and a waiting one names its notification.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: thread waits on something that is not a notification
Report: thread without a process is not stopped

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -456,7 +456,6 @@ static bool thread_stop(struct thread *t)
         unwait(t);
         t->frame.pc -= CALL_SIZE;
     }
-    t->state = THREAD_STOPPED;
     return core_thread_stopped(t);
 }
 
